{"model":"gpt-6-luna","messages":[{"role":"system","content":"## System Instructions\n\nGiven a question and context, answer step-by-step.\nIf unsure, answer \"Unknown\".\n\n## Tool Use\n\nUse the provided tool `extracted_data` to extract correct and accurate structured data from the input.\n\nTool purpose: Function call based on user instructions.\n\nCall the tool with the best supported arguments for the requested extraction."},{"role":"user","content":"<question>\nWould Arnold Schwarzenegger have been able to deadlift an adult Black rhinoceros at his peak strength?\n<\/question>\n<context>\nThe question asks for Arnold Schwarzenegger\u2019s peak deadlift. Publicly repeated accounts commonly cite a 675 lb (about 306 kg) deadlift, but this is not a well-documented official powerlifting record; present it as a reported lift rather than a verified competition maximum.\nArnold Schwarzenegger is commonly credited with a deadlift of about 675 lb (306 kg) during his bodybuilding prime. Treat this as a reported gym lift, not a verified official meet record; a reliably documented maximum is difficult to establish.\nIdentify the typical adult body-mass range for the black rhinoceros (Diceros bicornis), expressed in kilograms and optionally pounds.\nAdult black rhinoceroses typically weigh about 800\u20131,400 kg (1,760\u20133,090 lb).\nIdentify a reliable peak deadlift estimate for Arnold Schwarzenegger, compare it with adult black rhinoceros mass, and distinguish lifting an equivalent load from lifting an actual rhino. Arnold\u2019s commonly reported best deadlift is about 710 lb (322 kg), though historical strength figures vary. Adult black rhinos typically weigh roughly 1,760\u20133,080 lb (800\u20131,400 kg), around 2.5\u20134.3 times that load. Thus, he could not deadlift a typical adult black rhino; the animal is not a manageable stationary barbell load and would exceed the reported lift substantially.\nArnold Schwarzenegger\u2019s reported peak deadlift was about 710 lb (322 kg). An adult black rhinoceros typically weighs about 1,760\u20133,080 lb (800\u20131,400 kg), so it weighs roughly 2.5\u20134.3 times as much. He could not deadlift an adult black rhino: even an equivalent, evenly distributed barbell load would far exceed his reported maximum, and an actual rhino would be an impractical, unsafe, and moving load.\n<\/context>"}],"max_completion_tokens":1024,"tools":[{"type":"function","function":{"name":"extracted_data","description":"Function call based on user instructions.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"intermediate_reasoning":{"type":"string"},"correct_answer":{"type":"string"}},"required":["intermediate_reasoning","correct_answer"],"additionalProperties":false}}}],"tool_choice":{"type":"function","function":{"name":"extracted_data"}},"reasoning_effort":"none"}